  "description": "<h2><b>Towards site-specific nutrient management strategies: an open database in Senegal</b></h2><p><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\">Federico Gomez<sup>1*</sup>, Ana Carcedo<sup>1#</sup>, Andre Diatta<sup>2</sup>, Pape Djighaly<sup>3</sup>, Latha Nagarajan<sup>4</sup>, Upendra Singh<sup>4</sup>, Zachary Stewart<sup>5</sup>, Shamie Zingore<sup>6</sup>, Kaushik Majumdar<sup>6</sup>, P.V. Vara Prasad<sup>1</sup> and Ignacio Ciampitti<sup>1,7*</sup></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><sup>1</sup> Department of Agronomy, Kansas State University, Manhattan, Kansas, USA.<br><sup>2</sup> Department of Agronomy, Gaston Berger University, Saint-Louis, Senegal.<br><sup>3</sup> Department of Agroforestry, Assane Seck University, Ziguinchor, Senegal.<br><sup>4</sup> International Fertilizer Development Center, Washington DC, USA.<br><sup>5</sup> Center for Agriculture-Led Growth, Bureau for Resilience and Food Security, United States Agency for International Development, Washington, DC, USA.</p><p dir=\"ltr\"><sup>6</sup> African Plant Nutrition Institute (APNI), Ben Guerir, Morocco.<br><sup>7</sup> Department of Agronomy, Purdue University, West Lafayette, Indiana, USA.</p><p dir=\"ltr\"># Currently at: Plant Sciences Department, North Dakota State University, Fargo, North Dakota, USA.</p><p dir=\"ltr\">For more information about the dataset, please contact the corresponding authors at: fmgomez@ksu.edu, iciampit@purdue.edu.</p>",
